course: dictionary
lesson: 14959
title: Formal words: relinquish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Relinquish is a formal word, the kind you often find in stories, news reports and exam papers. It means to give something up, or to let go of it. «He relinquished his position as captain.» This means he gave up being captain.
explain: In everyday speech we say give up or hand over. If you let go of a rope, you relinquish your grip on it. A ruler who stops being in charge has relinquished power.
explain: Look for clues. Relinquish is usually followed by something you had, such as control, power or a grip. Often the person did not want to give it up, but had to. Ask yourself: did they give something up, or let it go?
fact: Relinquish means to give up something you have, or to let go of something you are holding.
fact: Relinquish is a formal word. Give up and hand over are everyday words with a similar meaning.
fact: «Relinquish control» means to stop being in charge.
fact: «The king relinquished the throne» means the king gave up his throne, often because he had to.
fact: Relinquish is a verb, so it changes: relinquishes, relinquished, relinquishing.
exercise: «She would not relinquish her grip on the rope.» What does relinquish mean here? | Pull the rope faster | Tie into a knot | Hold on tighter to | *Let go of
exercise: «The king relinquished the throne.» What does this mean? | *The king gave up his throne | The king sat on the throne all day | The king built a new throne | The king painted the throne gold
exercise: Which phrase means the same as «relinquish control»? | Control the traffic | Lose a game of chess | Take more control | *Stop being in charge
test: «He relinquished his position as captain.» Which everyday words could replace relinquished here? | Measured | Celebrated | *Gave up | Painted
test: «The mayor refused to relinquish power, even when the people asked.» What does relinquish power mean? | Win a prize | *Give up being in charge | Count the votes | Shout louder at the meeting
exam: «After many years, the old queen finally relinquished control of the kingdom to her son.» What does relinquished control mean? | Painted the castle walls | Took full control of the army | *Gave up being in charge of the kingdom | Argued about the kingdom's laws
